{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdUZtxwgke9sWMiCHLXs7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RMUNx8s18xpY4mHZFJchdu","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver/docs/aws-edge-integration.md","old_string":"### The contract with the edge\n\n| Public port (edge) | → home listener | PROXY variant |\n|---|---|---|\n| 25 (postscreen) | `10025` (or as tutorial defines) | `send-proxy` (v1) |\n| 587 submission | `10587` | `send-proxy` |\n| 465 smtps | `10465` | `send-proxy` |\n| 993 imaps | `10993` | `send-proxy-v2` |\n| 143 imap | `10143` | `send-proxy-v2` |\n\nHAProxy uses `send-proxy` for Postfix backends and `send-proxy-v2` for Dovecot. Keep these\nport numbers in lockstep with `aws/mail-edge` HAProxy config — they are the seam.\n\n## Network / tunnel\n\n- Home runs a **WireGuard** peer dialling out to the edge (outbound UDP 51820 is not\n  ISP-blocked). `PersistentKeepalive = 25` so the NAT mapping stays open.\n- DMS's proxy-protocol listeners only need to be reachable **from the tunnel**, not the LAN or\n  internet. Bind/firewall accordingly.\n- `haproxy_trusted_networks` (Dovecot) and Postfix's implicit trust must name the **edge's\n  tunnel IP** — if that's wrong, PROXY headers are ignored or spoofable.","new_string":"### The contract with the edge (as built)\n\nThere is **no port remapping**. `mailserver` shares `mail-edge-wg`'s network namespace\n(`network_mode: service:mail-edge-wg` in `docker-compose.yml`) instead of publishing host\nports, so Postfix/Dovecot bind `25/465/587/993` directly inside that netns — with no\nconflict against Traefik, which still owns `0.0.0.0:{25,465,587,993}` on the host for\nanything not going through the tunnel.\n\n| Public port (edge) | → home listener | PROXY variant |\n|---|---|---|\n| 25 (postscreen) | `25` | `send-proxy-v2` |\n| 587 submission | `587` | `send-proxy-v2` |\n| 465 smtps | `465` | `send-proxy-v2` |\n| 993 imaps | `993` | `send-proxy-v2` |\n\nHAProxy on the edge sends `send-proxy-v2` uniformly to all four. Port 143 (plain IMAP) is\n**not** proxied or exposed — it stays bound inside the netns, unreachable from the LAN or\ninternet, so it needs no PROXY listener. Keep this table in lockstep with the `aws/mail-edge`\nHAProxy config — it's the seam.\n\n## Network / tunnel\n\n- WireGuard runs as its **own container**, `mail-edge-wg` (`lscr.io/linuxserver/wireguard`),\n  not as a host-level `wg-quick@wg0` unit — this host has no passwordless sudo, so an\n  autonomous worker cannot install a systemd unit. The container owns the network namespace\n  that `mailserver` joins via `network_mode: service:mail-edge-wg`; wg0/10.77.0.2 exists only\n  inside that netns. Consequence: restarting `mail-edge-wg` destroys the namespace and\n  `mailserver` must be restarted after it — Docker will not cascade that restart on its own.\n  A `depends_on: condition: service_healthy` plus a healthcheck that checks for a live `wg0`\n  (not just an open port) exists in `docker-compose.yml` to catch that failure mode.\n- Home dials **out** to the edge (outbound UDP 51820, not ISP-blocked); the edge can never\n  initiate, since home sits behind NAT on a dynamic residential IP. `PersistentKeepalive = 25`\n  keeps the NAT mapping open. Peer config lives at\n  `~/projects/secrets/mail-edge-wg.conf` (mode 600), generated by `aws/mail-edge`.\n- `haproxy_trusted_networks` (Dovecot, `config/dovecot.cf`) is scoped to `10.77.0.1/32` — the\n  edge's tunnel IP only. Postfix's proxy directives (`config/postfix-master.cf`) are scoped\n  per-listener rather than global, so the internal amavis reinjection listener on 127.0.0.1\n  never gets stuck demanding a PROXY header it will never receive."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1112,"cache_read_input_tokens":71025,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1112},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4887fea5-78a1-4b14-a071-ae362ca71a13","uuid":"2e793e5d-f661-4aaa-8842-48639df4d5fc","timestamp":"2026-07-28T13:54:11.467Z","request_id":"req_011CdUZtwbaDyo9q4MPi6o7i"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RMUNx8s18xpY4mHZFJchdu","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver/docs/aws-edge-integration.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4887fea5-78a1-4b14-a071-ae362ca71a13","uuid":"8e2fc4dc-f115-40dd-9b0d-2941395c09c3","timestamp":"2026-07-28T13:54:11.530Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver/docs/aws-edge-integration.md","oldString":"### The contract with the edge\n\n| Public port (edge) | → home listener | PROXY variant |\n|---|---|---|\n| 25 (postscreen) | `10025` (or as tutorial defines) | `send-proxy` (v1) |\n| 587 submission | `10587` | `send-proxy` |\n| 465 smtps | `10465` | `send-proxy` |\n| 993 imaps | `10993` | `send-proxy-v2` |\n| 143 imap | `10143` | `send-proxy-v2` |\n\nHAProxy uses `send-proxy` for Postfix backends and `send-proxy-v2` for Dovecot. Keep these\nport numbers in lockstep with `aws/mail-edge` HAProxy config — they are the seam.\n\n## Network / tunnel\n\n- Home runs a **WireGuard** peer dialling out to the edge (outbound UDP 51820 is not\n  ISP-blocked). `PersistentKeepalive = 25` so the NAT mapping stays open.\n- DMS's proxy-protocol listeners only need to be reachable **from the tunnel**, not the LAN or\n  internet. Bind/firewall accordingly.\n- `haproxy_trusted_networks` (Dovecot) and Postfix's implicit trust must name the **edge's\n  tunnel IP** — if that's wrong, PROXY headers are ignored or spoofable.","newString":"### The contract with the edge (as built)\n\nThere is **no port remapping**. `mailserver` shares `mail-edge-wg`'s network namespace\n(`network_mode: service:mail-edge-wg` in `docker-compose.yml`) instead of publishing host\nports, so Postfix/Dovecot bind `25/465/587/993` directly inside that netns — with no\nconflict against Traefik, which still owns `0.0.0.0:{25,465,587,993}` on the host for\nanything not going through the tunnel.\n\n| Public port (edge) | → home listener | PROXY variant |\n|---|---|---|\n| 25 (postscreen) | `25` | `send-proxy-v2` |\n| 587 submission | `587` | `send-proxy-v2` |\n| 465 smtps | `465` | `send-proxy-v2` |\n| 993 imaps | `993` | `send-proxy-v2` |\n\nHAProxy on the edge sends `send-proxy-v2` uniformly to all four. Port 143 (plain IMAP) is\n**not** proxied or exposed — it stays bound inside the netns, unreachable from the LAN or\ninternet, so it needs no PROXY listener. Keep this table in lockstep with the `aws/mail-edge`\nHAProxy config — it's the seam.\n\n## Network / tunnel\n\n- WireGuard runs as its **own container**, `mail-edge-wg` (`lscr.io/linuxserver/wireguard`),\n  not as a host-level `wg-quick@wg0` unit — this host has no passwordless sudo, so an\n  autonomous worker cannot install a systemd unit. The container owns the network namespace\n  that `mailserver` joins via `network_mode: service:mail-edge-wg`; wg0/10.77.0.2 exists only\n  inside that netns. Consequence: restarting `mail-edge-wg` destroys the namespace and\n  `mailserver` must be restarted after it — Docker will not cascade that restart on its own.\n  A `depends_on: condition: service_healthy` plus a healthcheck that checks for a live `wg0`\n  (not just an open port) exists in `docker-compose.yml` to catch that failure mode.\n- Home dials **out** to the edge (outbound UDP 51820, not ISP-blocked); the edge can never\n  initiate, since home sits behind NAT on a dynamic residential IP. `PersistentKeepalive = 25`\n  keeps the NAT mapping open. Peer config lives at\n  `~/projects/secrets/mail-edge-wg.conf` (mode 600), generated by `aws/mail-edge`.\n- `haproxy_trusted_networks` (Dovecot, `config/dovecot.cf`) is scoped to `10.77.0.1/32` — the\n  edge's tunnel IP only. Postfix's proxy directives (`config/postfix-master.cf`) are scoped\n  per-listener rather than global, so the internal amavis reinjection listener on 127.0.0.1\n  never gets stuck demanding a PROXY header it will never receive.","originalFile":"# Running behind the AWS mail-edge\n\nHow this `docker-mailserver` (DMS) stack works when its public ports are terminated on an\nAWS edge and tunnelled home, instead of being exposed directly. The **AWS half** lives in\n[`~/projects/aws/mail-edge/README.md`](/home/administrator/projects/aws/mail-edge/README.md);\nread both — they are one system.\n\n## Why this is needed\n\nHome is on **Verizon residential**: inbound 25 is blocked, the IP is dynamic, and it's on the\nSpamhaus PBL so outbound mail is rejected. The AWS edge gives us a public Elastic IP with\nreverse DNS. DMS stays the **single source of truth** for all mail config; AWS is a dumb pipe.\n\n## The one thing that must change here: PROXY protocol\n\nIf the edge just TCP-forwards, DMS would see **every** connection as coming from the edge's\ntunnel IP — breaking Rspamd scoring, greylisting, and Fail2ban (they'd all act on one IP).\nThe fix is **PROXY protocol**: HAProxy on the edge prepends the real client IP, and DMS is\nconfigured to trust and read it. Postfix and Dovecot both support it. [DMS tutorial][dmsproxy]\n\n> ⚠️ **Verify exact directives against the current DMS tutorial before applying** — DMS is on\n> v15.x and the override filenames/port numbers below track the *edge/latest* \"Mail Server\n> behind a Proxy\" doc. There's also an open request to make this env-var-driven ([#3866][iss]),\n> so a newer DMS may simplify it. Treat the shapes below as the design, not copy-paste.\n\n### Postfix — `config/postfix-main.cf` + `config/postfix-master.cf`\n\n- Port 25 goes through `postscreen`, so enable proxy protocol there:\n  - `postfix-main.cf`: `postscreen_upstream_proxy_protocol = haproxy`\n  - `postfix-master.cf`: `smtp/inet/postscreen_upstream_proxy_protocol=haproxy`\n- Submission/SMTPS read it directly:\n  - `submission/inet/smtpd_upstream_proxy_protocol=haproxy`\n  - `smtps/inet/smtpd_upstream_proxy_protocol=haproxy`\n\n### Dovecot — `config/dovecot.cf`\n\n- `haproxy_trusted_networks = <edge WireGuard tunnel IP>` (trust ONLY the tunnel peer)\n- `haproxy_timeout = 3 secs`\n- Add PROXY-protocol `inet_listener`s on the dedicated ports the edge targets\n  (tutorial uses `10143` for imap, `10993` for imaps) with `haproxy = yes`.\n\n### The contract with the edge\n\n| Public port (edge) | → home listener | PROXY variant |\n|---|---|---|\n| 25 (postscreen) | `10025` (or as tutorial defines) | `send-proxy` (v1) |\n| 587 submission | `10587` | `send-proxy` |\n| 465 smtps | `10465` | `send-proxy` |\n| 993 imaps | `10993` | `send-proxy-v2` |\n| 143 imap | `10143` | `send-proxy-v2` |\n\nHAProxy uses `send-proxy` for Postfix backends and `send-proxy-v2` for Dovecot. Keep these\nport numbers in lockstep with `aws/mail-edge` HAProxy config — they are the seam.\n\n## Network / tunnel\n\n- Home runs a **WireGuard** peer dialling out to the edge (outbound UDP 51820 is not\n  ISP-blocked). `PersistentKeepalive = 25` so the NAT mapping stays open.\n- DMS's proxy-protocol listeners only need to be reachable **from the tunnel**, not the LAN or\n  internet. Bind/firewall accordingly.\n- `haproxy_trusted_networks` (Dovecot) and Postfix's implicit trust must name the **edge's\n  tunnel IP** — if that's wrong, PROXY headers are ignored or spoofable.\n\n## DNS (public `ai-servicers.com`)\n\n| Record | Value | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| MX | `mail.ai-servicers.com` pri 10 | receivers connect here → Elastic IP |\n| `mail` A | Elastic IP | set in `aws/mail-edge` |\n| PTR | `mail.ai-servicers.com` | **AWS-side**, via the port-25 form — not ours to set |\n| SPF | `v=spf1 mx -all` (or `ip4:<EIP> -all`) | authorise the edge IP as sender |\n| DKIM | generated by DMS (`setup config dkim`) | publish the TXT it emits |\n| DMARC | `v=DMARC1; p=quarantine; rua=mailto:postmaster@ai-servicers.com` | start at `p=none` to monitor |\n\n## Accounts\n\nMailboxes/domains via **postfixadmin** (already in the compose) or `setup email add`. Nothing\nabout account management changes under the edge.\n\n## Test plan (before trusting it)\n\n1. **Tunnel up:** `wg show` both ends; ping tunnel IPs.\n2. **Receive:** from an external account, mail to a test mailbox; confirm delivery.\n3. **Real IP preserved:** check `Received:` headers + Rspamd logs show the *sender's* IP, not\n   the edge tunnel IP. This is the whole point — if it shows the tunnel IP, PROXY protocol is\n   misconfigured.\n4. **Send:** `swaks --to you@gmail.com --from test@ai-servicers.com --server <tunnel>` ; confirm\n   it leaves via the edge (outbound 25 must be unblocked first) and lands in inbox, not spam.\n5. **Deliverability:** mail-tester.com / check SPF+DKIM+DMARC all pass, PTR matches (`dig -x`).\n6. **Fail2ban:** confirm it bans on the real client IP, not the tunnel.\n\n## Current stack state (2026-07-09)\n\n- `mailserver` + `postfixadmin` containers are **defined but not running** (not in `docker ps -a`).\n- Traefik currently holds 25/465/587/993 on the host. Under this design those move to the AWS\n  edge / WireGuard path — **decide** whether Traefik keeps any mail port locally or steps out.\n- No PROXY-protocol config present yet.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Docker Mailserver — Mail Server behind a Proxy][dmsproxy]\n- [DMS issue #3866 — PROXY protocol via env (future simplification)][iss]\n\n[dmsproxy]: https://docker-mailserver.github.io/docker-mailserver/edge/examples/tutorials/mailserver-behind-proxy/\n[iss]: https://github.com/docker-mailserver/docker-mailserver/issues/3866\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":39,"oldLines":27,"newStart":39,"newLines":44,"lines":[" - Add PROXY-protocol `inet_listener`s on the dedicated ports the edge targets","   (tutorial uses `10143` for imap, `10993` for imaps) with `haproxy = yes`."," ","-### The contract with the edge","+### The contract with the edge (as built)"," ","+There is **no port remapping**. `mailserver` shares `mail-edge-wg`'s network namespace","+(`network_mode: service:mail-edge-wg` in `docker-compose.yml`) instead of publishing host","+ports, so Postfix/Dovecot bind `25/465/587/993` directly inside that netns — with no","+conflict against Traefik, which still owns `0.0.0.0:{25,465,587,993}` on the host for","+anything not going through the tunnel.","+"," | Public port (edge) | → home listener | PROXY variant |"," |---|---|---|","-| 25 (postscreen) | `10025` (or as tutorial defines) | `send-proxy` (v1) |","-| 587 submission | `10587` | `send-proxy` |","-| 465 smtps | `10465` | `send-proxy` |","-| 993 imaps | `10993` | `send-proxy-v2` |","-| 143 imap | `10143` | `send-proxy-v2` |","+| 25 (postscreen) | `25` | `send-proxy-v2` |","+| 587 submission | `587` | `send-proxy-v2` |","+| 465 smtps | `465` | `send-proxy-v2` |","+| 993 imaps | `993` | `send-proxy-v2` |"," ","-HAProxy uses `send-proxy` for Postfix backends and `send-proxy-v2` for Dovecot. Keep these","-port numbers in lockstep with `aws/mail-edge` HAProxy config — they are the seam.","+HAProxy on the edge sends `send-proxy-v2` uniformly to all four. Port 143 (plain IMAP) is","+**not** proxied or exposed — it stays bound inside the netns, unreachable from the LAN or","+internet, so it needs no PROXY listener. Keep this table in lockstep with the `aws/mail-edge`","+HAProxy config — it's the seam."," "," ## Network / tunnel"," ","-- Home runs a **WireGuard** peer dialling out to the edge (outbound UDP 51820 is not","-  ISP-blocked). `PersistentKeepalive = 25` so the NAT mapping stays open.","-- DMS's proxy-protocol listeners only need to be reachable **from the tunnel**, not the LAN or","-  internet. Bind/firewall accordingly.","-- `haproxy_trusted_networks` (Dovecot) and Postfix's implicit trust must name the **edge's","-  tunnel IP** — if that's wrong, PROXY headers are ignored or spoofable.","+- WireGuard runs as its **own container**, `mail-edge-wg` (`lscr.io/linuxserver/wireguard`),","+  not as a host-level `wg-quick@wg0` unit — this host has no passwordless sudo, so an","+  autonomous worker cannot install a systemd unit. The container owns the network namespace","+  that `mailserver` joins via `network_mode: service:mail-edge-wg`; wg0/10.77.0.2 exists only","+  inside that netns. Consequence: restarting `mail-edge-wg` destroys the namespace and","+  `mailserver` must be restarted after it — Docker will not cascade that restart on its own.","+  A `depends_on: condition: service_healthy` plus a healthcheck that checks for a live `wg0`","+  (not just an open port) exists in `docker-compose.yml` to catch that failure mode.","+- Home dials **out** to the edge (outbound UDP 51820, not ISP-blocked); the edge can never","+  initiate, since home sits behind NAT on a dynamic residential IP. `PersistentKeepalive = 25`","+  keeps the NAT mapping open. Peer config lives at","+  `~/projects/secrets/mail-edge-wg.conf` (mode 600), generated by `aws/mail-edge`.","+- `haproxy_trusted_networks` (Dovecot, `config/dovecot.cf`) is scoped to `10.77.0.1/32` — the","+  edge's tunnel IP only. Postfix's proxy directives (`config/postfix-master.cf`) are scoped","+  per-listener rather than global, so the internal amavis reinjection listener on 127.0.0.1","+  never gets stuck demanding a PROXY header it will never receive."," "," ## DNS (public `ai-servicers.com`)"," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
