{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CQp7cidYcxECPx7UPDfLNM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Docker-Mailserver Project\n2\t\n3\t> 🔀 **Session history (refocus)**: See [docs/refocus/INDEX.md](docs/refocus/INDEX.md) for incoming briefs and outbound spawns.\n4\t\n5\t## Current Status (2026-07-28): AWS edge live, MX not yet cut over\n6\t\n7\tThe stack was rebuilt behind an AWS edge (`~/projects/aws/mail-edge/`, Elastic IP\n8\t`34.194.247.228`) because Verizon residential blocks inbound port 25 and lacks IP reputation\n9\tfor outbound delivery. See [`docs/aws-edge-integration.md`](docs/aws-edge-integration.md) for\n10\tthe full design, verified log evidence, and open items — this section is the summary.\n11\t\n12\t- `mailserver` and `mail-edge-wg` (containerized WireGuard peer) are both **up and healthy**.\n13\t  `mailserver` joins `mail-edge-wg`'s network namespace via `network_mode:\n14\t  service:mail-edge-wg` — it has no `networks:`/`ports:`/Traefik labels of its own; restarting\n15\t  `mail-edge-wg` destroys that namespace and requires restarting `mailserver` afterward.\n16\t- PROXY protocol (HAProxy v2) is configured on Postfix (`config/postfix-master.cf`, scoped\n17\t  per-listener) and Dovecot (`config/dovecot.cf`, `haproxy_trusted_networks = 10.77.0.1/32`)\n18\t  for all four edge-forwarded ports: 25, 465, 587, 993. **Verified working** — DMS logs show\n19\t  the real client IP end-to-end, not the tunnel peer's.\n20\t- **MX for `ai-servicers.com` still points at Cloudflare Email Routing.** No production mail\n21\t  flows through this edge yet; cutover is a deliberate, separate human decision (not\n22\t  automated). `mail.ai-servicers.com` currently resolves to the Elastic IP with Cloudflare's\n23\t  proxy off, and was removed from `ddns-updater` so nothing overwrites it.\n24\t- The Elastic IP's PTR record is still **pending** at AWS — do not send test mail to\n25\t  third-party domains (Gmail, Outlook, etc.) until it resolves.\n26\t- Legacy direct-Traefik-routing setup described below (SSL mount, Traefik TCP routing) is\n27\t  **superseded** by the edge/tunnel path for anything reaching the mail ports via WireGuard;\n28\t  Traefik still holds those host ports for non-edge traffic, but production intent is the edge.\n29\t\n30\t### Mail Accounts"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4887fea5-78a1-4b14-a071-ae362ca71a13","uuid":"dc93661d-ae76-49d4-a23b-6e4bea195ecf","timestamp":"2026-07-28T14:01:47.539Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver/CLAUDE.md","content":"# Docker-Mailserver Project\n\n> 🔀 **Session history (refocus)**: See [docs/refocus/INDEX.md](docs/refocus/INDEX.md) for incoming briefs and outbound spawns.\n\n## Current Status (2026-07-28): AWS edge live, MX not yet cut over\n\nThe stack was rebuilt behind an AWS edge (`~/projects/aws/mail-edge/`, Elastic IP\n`34.194.247.228`) because Verizon residential blocks inbound port 25 and lacks IP reputation\nfor outbound delivery. See [`docs/aws-edge-integration.md`](docs/aws-edge-integration.md) for\nthe full design, verified log evidence, and open items — this section is the summary.\n\n- `mailserver` and `mail-edge-wg` (containerized WireGuard peer) are both **up and healthy**.\n  `mailserver` joins `mail-edge-wg`'s network namespace via `network_mode:\n  service:mail-edge-wg` — it has no `networks:`/`ports:`/Traefik labels of its own; restarting\n  `mail-edge-wg` destroys that namespace and requires restarting `mailserver` afterward.\n- PROXY protocol (HAProxy v2) is configured on Postfix (`config/postfix-master.cf`, scoped\n  per-listener) and Dovecot (`config/dovecot.cf`, `haproxy_trusted_networks = 10.77.0.1/32`)\n  for all four edge-forwarded ports: 25, 465, 587, 993. **Verified working** — DMS logs show\n  the real client IP end-to-end, not the tunnel peer's.\n- **MX for `ai-servicers.com` still points at Cloudflare Email Routing.** No production mail\n  flows through this edge yet; cutover is a deliberate, separate human decision (not\n  automated). `mail.ai-servicers.com` currently resolves to the Elastic IP with Cloudflare's\n  proxy off, and was removed from `ddns-updater` so nothing overwrites it.\n- The Elastic IP's PTR record is still **pending** at AWS — do not send test mail to\n  third-party domains (Gmail, Outlook, etc.) until it resolves.\n- Legacy direct-Traefik-routing setup described below (SSL mount, Traefik TCP routing) is\n  **superseded** by the edge/tunnel path for anything reaching the mail ports via WireGuard;\n  Traefik still holds those host ports for non-edge traffic, but production intent is the edge.\n\n### Mail Accounts","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":254}}}
