{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdUagHEGtZU5P1aUd8ULZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HJM2bfBYL8K3KfD7PML4bf","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver/docs/context/architecture.md","content":"# Architecture\n\n## Components\n- `mailserver` — `ghcr.io/docker-mailserver/docker-mailserver:latest`. [IMPLEMENTED] Runs with\n  `network_mode: service:mail-edge-wg` — no `networks:`, `ports:`, or Docker labels of its own.\n  It shares the network namespace of `mail-edge-wg` instead of attaching directly to\n  `mailserver-net`/`traefik-net`.\n- `mail-edge-wg` — `lscr.io/linuxserver/wireguard`. [IMPLEMENTED] Containerized WireGuard peer\n  that owns the shared netns. Dials out to the AWS mail edge (Elastic IP `34.194.247.228`,\n  endpoint `:51820`); home never receives inbound WireGuard connections (dynamic residential\n  IP behind NAT). Tunnel addresses: edge `10.77.0.1`, home `10.77.0.2`.\n- `postfixadmin` — profile-gated (`profiles: [\"postfixadmin\"]`), on `mailserver-net` +\n  `traefik-net` directly (not affected by the netns change); reaches mail via\n  `mail-edge-wg:25` since that's the only DNS name in the shared netns.\n\n## Data flow (mail edge path)\n1. External client → `34.194.247.228:{25,465,587,993}` (AWS HAProxy).\n2. HAProxy prepends a PROXY protocol v2 header with the real client IP, forwards over\n   WireGuard to `10.77.0.2:{25,465,587,993}`.\n3. Postfix (`postscreen` on 25, `smtpd` on 587/465) and Dovecot (`imap-login` on 993) read the\n   PROXY header and log/score/authenticate against the real client IP, not the tunnel peer.\n\n## Known gap\n- [BROKEN] Traefik's TCP routing to mail (previously Docker-label-discovered on `mailserver`)\n  has no backend now that those labels don't exist. See `gotchas.md`.\n\n## See also\n- `docs/aws-edge-integration.md` — full edge design + verified evidence.\n- `docs/refocus/2026-07-28-proxy-protocol-edge-ca1077.md` — the session that built this.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1023,"cache_read_input_tokens":147904,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1023},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4887fea5-78a1-4b14-a071-ae362ca71a13","uuid":"61f654e2-d8f8-4e2f-84d1-7535e7e24419","timestamp":"2026-07-28T14:04:20.675Z","request_id":"req_011CdUagDDBTeWBDaC5KZWYS"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HJM2bfBYL8K3KfD7PML4bf","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver/docs/context/architecture.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4887fea5-78a1-4b14-a071-ae362ca71a13","uuid":"12a006a7-0be4-44a9-8287-3560caf03acb","timestamp":"2026-07-28T14:04:20.708Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver/docs/context/architecture.md","content":"# Architecture\n\n## Components\n- `mailserver` — `ghcr.io/docker-mailserver/docker-mailserver:latest`. [IMPLEMENTED] Runs with\n  `network_mode: service:mail-edge-wg` — no `networks:`, `ports:`, or Docker labels of its own.\n  It shares the network namespace of `mail-edge-wg` instead of attaching directly to\n  `mailserver-net`/`traefik-net`.\n- `mail-edge-wg` — `lscr.io/linuxserver/wireguard`. [IMPLEMENTED] Containerized WireGuard peer\n  that owns the shared netns. Dials out to the AWS mail edge (Elastic IP `34.194.247.228`,\n  endpoint `:51820`); home never receives inbound WireGuard connections (dynamic residential\n  IP behind NAT). Tunnel addresses: edge `10.77.0.1`, home `10.77.0.2`.\n- `postfixadmin` — profile-gated (`profiles: [\"postfixadmin\"]`), on `mailserver-net` +\n  `traefik-net` directly (not affected by the netns change); reaches mail via\n  `mail-edge-wg:25` since that's the only DNS name in the shared netns.\n\n## Data flow (mail edge path)\n1. External client → `34.194.247.228:{25,465,587,993}` (AWS HAProxy).\n2. HAProxy prepends a PROXY protocol v2 header with the real client IP, forwards over\n   WireGuard to `10.77.0.2:{25,465,587,993}`.\n3. Postfix (`postscreen` on 25, `smtpd` on 587/465) and Dovecot (`imap-login` on 993) read the\n   PROXY header and log/score/authenticate against the real client IP, not the tunnel peer.\n\n## Known gap\n- [BROKEN] Traefik's TCP routing to mail (previously Docker-label-discovered on `mailserver`)\n  has no backend now that those labels don't exist. See `gotchas.md`.\n\n## See also\n- `docs/aws-edge-integration.md` — full edge design + verified evidence.\n- `docs/refocus/2026-07-28-proxy-protocol-edge-ca1077.md` — the session that built this.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdUah7GGvMMPbv8wDeQMy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LPvM7BK9A2HXdW5UCiPX2a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/administrator/projects/docker-mailserver/docs/context/operations.md","content":"# Operations\n\n## Restart semantics — mail-edge-wg / mailserver coupling\n- [IMPLEMENTED] Both containers are `restart: unless-stopped` and start in order via\n  `depends_on: condition: service_healthy` — this only orders *startup*, not ongoing recovery.\n- Restarting `mail-edge-wg` alone **destroys the shared network namespace**. `mailserver`\n  keeps running inside the now-orphaned netns rather than being restarted by Docker.\n- `mailserver`'s healthcheck checks for a live `wg0` inside its netns (not just an open port)\n  specifically to catch this — but detection ≠ recovery. **Manually restart `mailserver`**\n  after any `mail-edge-wg` restart.\n\n## Host reboot\n- [IMPLEMENTED] Both containers come back on host reboot via `restart: unless-stopped` (no\n  host-level `wg-quick@wg0` systemd unit — this host has no passwordless sudo for an\n  autonomous worker to install one).\n\n## Secrets\n- `~/projects/secrets/mail-edge-wg.conf` (mode 600) — WireGuard peer config, generated by\n  `~/projects/aws/mail-edge/`. `AllowedIPs = 10.77.0.0/24` — scoped to the tunnel subnet only,\n  so `mailserver`'s general internet egress (e.g. SendGrid relay) is unaffected.\n- `~/projects/secrets/docker-mailserver.env` — main env config (unchanged by this work).\n\n## DKIM key material\n- `config/opendkim/keys/` contains a private key readable only by `root` inside the container\n  (perm-denied for the `administrator` user). [IMPLEMENTED] `.gitignore`d as `config/opendkim/`\n  — never commit private key material.\n\n## Verification commands used\n```bash\ndocker logs mailserver 2>&1 | grep -i 'postscreen\\|submission.*smtpd\\|submissions.*smtpd\\|imap-login'\n# real client IP (e.g. 108.35.80.85) should appear, not 10.77.0.1\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":976,"cache_read_input_tokens":148927,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":976},"output_tokens":68,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4887fea5-78a1-4b14-a071-ae362ca71a13","uuid":"6acf4faf-af59-46b2-8f30-4c4c24d49ff8","timestamp":"2026-07-28T14:04:31.083Z","request_id":"req_011CdUah4nwqn113E71jKAEh"}
