{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdUakq16ASRE1hToRrWTp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Refocus brief closed out with status `result`. Here's the final state:\n\n| Decision | Rationale | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| WireGuard tunnel + PROXY protocol v2 on 25/465/587/993 | AWS edge already verified working from its side; home half needed docs to match reality | ✅ Verified independently this session — real client IP confirmed in Postfix + Dovecot logs on all four ports |\n| Corrected `docs/aws-edge-integration.md` port table | Old doc sketched a 10025-style remap that was never built | ✅ Done |\n| Corrected `CLAUDE.md` status | Was claiming \"FULLY OPERATIONAL\" while no container existed at brief start | ✅ Done |\n| Kept containerized WireGuard (not host `wg-quick`) | Parent already endorsed it; no passwordless sudo on host anyway | ✅ Documented, not re-litigated |\n| Traefik mail TCP routing regression | Advisor review caught a stale \"Nextcloud IMAP works\" claim I almost shipped; investigation proved it's now broken | 🔴 Confirmed broken, filed as follow-up for the `traefik` project — not fixed here (out of scope, 1-hop rule) |\n| `config/opendkim/` gitignored | DKIM private key was untracked and unreadable; must never be committed | ✅ Done |\n\n**Open decisions (for you or the traefik project owner):**\n1. Traefik no longer has a route to `mailserver` (labels are forbidden under `network_mode: service:*`) — `mail.ai-servicers.com:993`/`:587` currently return HTTP 400 instead of proxying IMAP/SMTP. This breaks Nextcloud Mail's existing integration. Needs a Traefik-side fix (new label source or file-provider route to `mail-edge-wg`).\n2. MX cutover from Cloudflare Email Routing to the AWS edge remains a deliberate, separate human decision — not touched here, per the brief's explicit guard.\n\n**Bottom line:** the edge/tunnel work itself is done and verified; the one thing it broke in the process (Traefik→mail routing) is now visible in docs and queued as a follow-up rather than silently left broken."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":459,"cache_read_input_tokens":153400,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":459},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4887fea5-78a1-4b14-a071-ae362ca71a13","uuid":"0d1202bf-70f6-4d8d-ad08-61745e69aedc","timestamp":"2026-07-28T14:05:24.408Z","request_id":"req_011CdUakhsiX2hcNwPScF4kJ"}
